<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67896" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μίνυνθ-ᾰ</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a short time</i>, in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> mostly in phrase, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. περ οὔ τι μάλα δήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.416
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				22.473
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. δέ οἱ γένεθ᾽ ὁρμή</span>
			but <i>short-lived</i> was his effort, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.466
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ πολλὸν ἐπὶ χρόνον, ἀλλὰ μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					15.494
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. δὲ γίγνεται ἥβης καρπός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Mimn.
					2.7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. δέ μοι ψυχὰ γλυκεῖα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					5.151
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν δ᾽ οὔτι μ. περ εὔνασεν ὕπνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.1060
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
